    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`). Here's what I implemented for the `bulkSignupWarning` rule.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe rule \u2014 *true once more than 80 owners have already been created on the same business day* \u2014 needed to be computed at create time and read back on GET, so I persist it on the `Owner` entity (like the existing `namesakeCount`), matching how the daily-limit rule accumulates per-day counts.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`FlagBulkSignupWarning.java`** (new function step) \u2014 counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the new owner's adjusted business day; sets `bulkSignupWarning = count > 80`. Runs before `SaveOwner` so the owner being created isn't counted, reusing the same per-day logic as `RequireDailyRegistrationLimit`.\n\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `bulkSignup` step into the pipeline between `namesakes` and `save`, under `govern: [ transaction ]`.\n\n3. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `bulkSignupWarning` (`Boolean`, column `bulk_signup_warning`) field with getter/setter. MapStruct's `OwnerMapper` maps it to/from `OwnerDto` automatically by name, so both POST and GET responses carry it.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `bulkSignupWarning` read-only boolean property to the `Owner` response schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it).\n\n5. **Schema/data** \u2014 added `bulk_signup_warning BOOLEAN` to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb/h2/postgres/mysql), and appended the trailing value to the positional owner `INSERT`s in the hsqldb `data.sql` (the test profile uses hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`; the other DBs use column-list inserts and needed no data change).\n\nThe acceptance test `coreNoBulkWarningUnderThreshold` (fresh create \u2192 `bulkSignupWarning` false) passes, as does the full suite.",
